# Authoritative compact recording addendum

This addendum applies only to the declared R10 initial and selected compact critic jobs and their pinned recording method. It explicitly overrides the unchanged rubric/review rules' instructions to write only two reports and to manually repeat required/normalized/comparison fields. Each critic instead exclusively creates exactly three expected report files: `PROFILE.observations.json`, then the declared adapter's deterministic `PROFILE.json` and `PROFILE.md`. This is a recording-only override. All seven quality dimensions and their existing integer scale, mandatory conditions, all-three floor of 4 in every dimension, full-set diversity floor of 4, exact count fidelity, source preservation, independent sessions, complete viewing, NA, and finite review rules remain authoritative and unchanged.

Read the complete pinned client request and packet without producer concepts, self-inspections, selection reasons, peer reviews, or earlier raw results. View every exact supplied source asset and read applicable protected-layout manifests first. View all five members in packet order, each at native/use/thumbnail: complete all fifteen poster views before beginning the first copy-reading/transcription stage or any judgment/score. Record the actual first raw reading of every supplied copy entry, once in packet order; never fill it from required text, normalize it in place, or infer invisible scene/text from intent. Every printable copy entry declared in this packet must be represented in each member's compact copy array. Do not presume printable copy from internal group names, field labels, or production explanation.

